<BaseLayout title="Primitive Challenges — The Moving Invariant"><section class="hero"><div class="eyebrow">Open challenge registry</div><h1>Show the remainder.</h1><p class="lede">The possibility of an undiscovered primitive remains a legitimate empirical possibility. It is not a standing refutation.</p></section><section><h2>What would count</h2><ul class="research-copy"><li>A seventh irreducible Transformation Pattern.</li><li>A fourth irreducible Completion Topology.</li><li>A fourth irreducible Persistence Mode.</li><li>Evidence that the three axes are not independent or exhaustive in the claimed way.</li><li>A completed unit that cannot receive a coordinate without residue after domain, grain and instrument errors are controlled.</li></ul></section><section><h2>What does not count by itself</h2><p class="research-copy">Additional semantic detail, causal history, imported speaker or institution, mechanism, subtype, grammatical construction, plurality, negation, purpose, scene, a synonym for an existing primitive, or the abstract claim that “there could always be more.”</p></section><section><h2>Open registry</h2><p>{challenges.length===0?'No primitive challenge has yet been recorded in this repository. The registry is ready for the first genuine candidate.':`${challenges.length} challenge(s) recorded.`}</p></section></BaseLayout>
